    "message": "feat(desktop): choose the window provider from the dashboard\n\n5.27.0 added a window preference to desktop.json and a --window flag, but the\ndashboard could not set it. The endpoint carried the value through every save\nwithout ever accepting one, so the only way to change it was the CLI.\n\nThe Deployment section already existed, so this adds a control to it rather\nthan building a second home for desktop settings. Beside the select, a\nread-only line reports what `auto` actually resolves to on this machine --\n\"auto → app-mode (Microsoft Edge)\" -- because a preference of \"auto\" otherwise\ntells you nothing about what you will get.\n\nEach option states its real consequence, and the embedded-webview option says\nplainly that OAuth login, downloads and copy buttons may not work in it. That\nis the reason app-mode is the default, so burying it would be the one thing\nthis hint must not do.\n\nResolution had to be readable from the API, and `api` may not import `cli`\n(tests/contracts/test_import_boundaries.py). Rather than crossing the edge or\nkeeping a second copy, the Chromium lookup and availability logic MOVED from\ncli/desktop_window.py to config/desktop.py, which both may import -- a\ncomplete migration, not a shim.\n\nAn unknown value is rejected with a 400 rather than silently defaulting, and\nan unrelated save still cannot reset the preference (that preservation is the\nregression this endpoint was already carrying a guard for; it now has a test).\n\nVerification:\n\n- Full suite: 6 failed, 4294 passed, 26 skipped -- the six documented\n  PowerShell installer failures, identical to unmodified fork/main measured in\n  the same shell. Zero new failures.\n- Import boundaries: 19 passed, so the move satisfies the declared policy.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n- Live server on a throwaway home, real HTTP: setting a value persists to\n  desktop.json and survives repeated unrelated saves; an invalid value returns\n  400 and does not stick; the resolved line reported \"app-mode\"/\"Microsoft\n  Edge\"; and the select is present in the served HTML, not merely in the\n  source.\n\nOne defect fixed on review. `_desktop_state_response` called\n`resolve_auto_window()` inline on an async handler. Measured 43 ms median and\n75 ms max, and it does not get cheaper on repeat because shutil.which is the\ncost rather than the import -- so every desktop request stalled the event loop\nfor that long. All three call sites now hand it to a thread, with the\nmeasurement recorded next to it.\n\nAlso worth recording, because it nearly produced a false bug report: a live\nreproduction \"showed\" the preference resetting on every unrelated save, and the\nsuite showed a matching seventh failure. Both were artifacts of starting a\nserver from the worktree venv while `uv run pytest` was reinstalling the\npackage into that same venv. Run with nothing else touching the venv, the\nbehaviour is correct and the suite is at baseline.\n\nNot verified: the dashboard was exercised over real HTTP against a running\nserver, but no DOM was executed -- the select's presence is asserted in the\nserved markup, not by running admin.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
